course: dictionary
lesson: 45
title: Accidentally: by mistake, not on purpose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Accidentally» means by accident, not on purpose. Look at the words around it to check. «I accidentally dropped my sandwich.» The clues are dropped and sandwich. Nobody plans to drop their lunch, so the word tells you it was not on purpose.
explain: Accidentally comes from accident, so the two words are related. An accident happens without meaning to make it happen. If you can swap in «by accident» and the sentence still makes sense, you have understood the word.
explain: Saying something happened accidentally does not mean you can forget it. «If you accidentally hurt a friend, stop, check they are okay and say sorry.» The word explains how it happened, but you still have to help put things right.
fact: Accidentally means by accident, not on purpose, without meaning to.
fact: Opposites of accidentally are on purpose, deliberately and intentionally.
fact: A good check is to swap in «by accident» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «I accidentally dropped my sandwich» means I did not mean to drop it.
fact: If you accidentally hurt someone, say sorry and check they are okay.
exercise: «I accidentally dropped my sandwich.» What does accidentally mean? | *By accident, not on purpose | On purpose, after planning it carefully | Again and again every day | Very quickly and very loudly
exercise: Which word means the opposite of accidentally? | Loudly | *Deliberately | By accident | Sadly
exercise: «If you accidentally hurt a friend, stop, check they are okay and say sorry.» What should you do after you accidentally hurt a friend? | Laugh so they know it was not a big deal | Walk away and say nothing | *Check they are okay and say sorry | Hurt them back so it is fair
test: Which sentence uses accidentally correctly? | Accidentally, the table is a big round shape. | I accidentally decided to knock my cup off the table on purpose. | *I accidentally knocked my cup off the table. | The accidentally dog ran across the park.
test: «Gwil notices and starts accidentally missing his shots.» What does accidentally tell you about the missed shots? | They were missed because the ball was very big | They were missed on purpose, as a trick | They were missed because Gwil was sleepy in class | *They were missed without meaning to
exam: Lily says, «I accidentally knocked over my drink,» and then helps mop up the spill. What does accidentally tell you? | It happened last week | It was done on purpose to make a mess | *It was not on purpose, so she did not mean to make a mess | She did it very loudly
